  "narrative": {
    "intro": "At and T Enterprises has $231M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $226M of that total. At and T Enterprises has 26 awards so far this fiscal year and an average award size of $8.9M. At and T Enterprises obligations are down 77.7% year over year. Historically, At and T Enterprises had larger multi-year activity: FY22 was $349M, FY23 was $778M, FY24 was $941M, FY25 was $1B, and FY26 was $1B. At and T Enterprises sales in FY2027 are concentrated in Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $231M, with Other Computer Related Services showing $0. Other named buying agencies include the Social Security Administration $2.2M, the Department of Justice $1.6M, the Department of Defense $921K, the General Services Administration $228K, the Department of Homeland Security $166K, the United States Trade and Development Agency $105K, the Executive Office of the President $50K, and the Department of the Treasury $0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of At and T Enterprises in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $226M in obligations. The Social Security Administration and the Department of Justice follow with $2.2M and $1.6M respectively. Other named agencies include the Department of Defense $921K and the General Services Administration $228K, with smaller reported amounts for other agencies."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are At and T Enterprises FY2027 obligations by market and legacy performance?",
        "body": "Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the reported market with $231M in obligations for FY2027 to date. Other Computer Related Services shows $0 in FY2027 obligations. Prior fiscal years were larger: FY22 $349M, FY23 $778M, FY24 $941M, FY25 $1B, and FY26 $1B."
      }
    ]
